  "content": {
    "title": "FuboTV to carry new BravesVision channel in 2026",
    "text": "SportsPublished: Mar. 27, 2026, 1:05 p.m.By Creg Stephenson | cstephenson@al.comThe Atlanta Braves have reached a multi-year agreement with FuboTV to carry the new BravesVision channel, it was announced Friday.BravesVision will broadcast more than 140 games in 2026, all except those set aside for national networks (NBC, ESPN, Fox/Fox Sports 1) and/or streaming packages (Apple TV, Peacock). Out-of-market consumers can continue to watch Braves games via MLB.tv.FuboTV is a streaming-only service that focuses on live sports. Fubo subscribers in the Braves’ broadcast “territory” (which includes all of Alabama) will receive BravesVision as part of their base subscription starting with Friday night’s season-opener vs. the Kansas City Royals (first pitch set for 6:15 p.m.).In addition to games, BravesVision will broadcast the “Braves on Deck” pre-game show and “Braves Postgame” show. The first pre-game show broadcast is set to air at 5 p.m. Central on Friday.RECOMMENDEDIn addition, fans who live in the Braves’ market may purchase the streaming-only BravesVision package for $19.99 per month or $99.99 per year. The Braves Vision streaming package has no blackout restrictions.A select number of Braves games will also be broadcast over the air by Gray Media, which has stations in all of Alabama’s television markets. To find out where “Braves on Gray” is available in your area, click HERE.The Braves previously announced similar agreements with two major cable outlets that serve the state of Alabama: Xfinity TV and Spectrum. Announcements regarding BravesVision and other cable, satellite and streaming providers are expected to be made in the coming days.",
    "word_count": 251,
    "extraction_method": "readability"
  },
